          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Injective and projective morphisms are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            satisfying some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+systems"} weak factorization systems
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#injective_and_projective Injective and projective
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset Mor(\mathcal{C})
            of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in Mor(\mathcal{C})
            is called
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  \-injective morphism
                if it has the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                against elements in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %li
              %p
                a
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  \-projective morphism
                if it has the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
                against elements in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            for which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∃
                      %mo !
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\exists!}{\to} \ast
            is a
            = succeed "-injective" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} injective object
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            has an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            for which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ∅
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∃
                      %mo !
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \stackrel{\exists!}{\to} X
            is a
            = succeed "-projective" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective object
          %h3#fibration_and_cofibration Fibration and cofibration
          %p Frequently one furthermore says:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"} cofibration
                is a morphism that has the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
                against all
                = succeed "-injective" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %li
              %p
                a
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
                is a morphism that has the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                against all
                = succeed "-projective" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#ClosureProperties Closure properties
          #ClosurePropertiesOfInjectiveAndProjectiveMorphisms.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\subset Mor(\mathcal{C})
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mi Proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mi Inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Inj
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+morphisms"} projective morphisms
              and of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphisms"} injective morphisms
              (the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+negation"}> Quillen negation
              ” of
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  Both classes contain the class of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  Both classes are closed under
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mi Proj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
                  is also closed under
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              %li
                %p
                  Both classes are closed under forming
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
                  in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mrow
                              %mi Δ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mi Proj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
                  is closed under forming
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
                  of morphisms in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  (“
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobase+change"}> cobase change
                  ”).
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mi Inj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Inj
                  is closed under forming
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                  of morphisms in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  (“
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"}> base change
                  ”).
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mi Proj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
                  is closed under forming
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mrow
                              %mi Δ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mi Inj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Inj
                  is closed under forming
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mrow
                              %mi Δ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p We go through each item in turn.
            %p
              %strong containing isomorphisms
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi Iso
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\overset{f}{\rightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}_{\mathllap{\in Iso}}^{\mathllap{i}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\underset{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              with the left morphism an isomorphism, the a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
              is given by using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
              of this isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo ∘
                          %msup
                            %mi i
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                      %mo ↗
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^{{f \circ i^{-1}}}\nearrow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in K
              and so
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                      %mi Proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in K Proj
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
            %p
              %strong closure under composition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                                  %mi Inj
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                                  %mi Inj
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_1}}_{\mathrlap{\in K Inj}}
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i}}_{\mathllap{\in K}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_2}}_{\mathrlap{\in K Inj}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              consider its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              decomposition as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                                  %mi Inj
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                                  %mi Inj
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \&amp;\searrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_1}}_{\mathrlap{\in K Inj}}
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i}}_{\mathllap{\in K}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_2}}_{\mathrlap{\in K Inj}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now the bottom commuting square has a lift, by assumption. This yields another
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              decomposition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                                  %mi Inj
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                                  %mi Inj
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i}}_{\mathllap{\in K}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_1}}_{\mathrlap{\in K Inj}}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\nearrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_2}}_{\mathrlap{\in K Inj}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              and now the top commuting square has a lift by assumption. This is now equivalently a lift in the total diagram, showing that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1\circ p_1
              has the right lifting property against
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              and is hence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mi Inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Inj
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mi Proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mi Proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
              under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              follows since the latter is given by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              of sequential composition and successive lifts against the underlying sequence as above constitutes a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            %p
              %strong closure under retracts
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              of an
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                      %mi Proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in K Proj
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of the form.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi A
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                                  %mi Proj
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi B
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    id_A \colon &amp; A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; C &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i}}_{\mathrlap{\in K Proj}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}}
                    \\\
                    id_B \colon &amp; B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; D &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; B
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p Then for
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{j}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in K}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              composite with that retract diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                                  %mi Proj
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; C &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i}}_{\mathrlap{\in K Proj}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in K}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; D &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; B &amp;\longrightarrow &amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p Now the pasting composite of the two squares on the right has a lift, by assumption,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                                  %mi Proj
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; C &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{i}}_{\mathrlap{\in K Proj}}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\nearrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in K}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; D &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; B &amp;\longrightarrow &amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By composition, this is also a lift in the total outer rectangle, hence in the original square. Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              has the left lifting property against all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in K
              and hence is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mi Proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} formally dual
            %p
              %strong closure under pushout and pullback
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mi Inj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in K Inj
              and and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi f
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Z \times_f X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{{f^* p}}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    Z &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow} &amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              diagram in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* p
              has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              with respect to all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in K
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi f
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msup
                                      %mi f
                                      %mo *
                                    %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Z \times_f X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i}}_{\mathllap{\in K}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\mathrlap{f^* p}}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\stackrel{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Z
                    }
            %p
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              composite with the pullback square from above to obtain the commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi f
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi p
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Z \times_f X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f^* p}}
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\stackrel{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Z &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the right lifting property of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi f
                                %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{i}} &amp;{}^{\hat {(f g)}}\nearrow&amp;  \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\stackrel{f g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              this gives rise to the lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat g
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi f
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mover
                                %mi g
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi p
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; Z \times_f X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \&amp;{}^{\hat g} \nearrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f^* p}}
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\stackrel{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Z &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              In order for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat g
              to qualify as the intended lift of the total diagram, it remains to show that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi f
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mover
                                %mi g
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo ↗
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Z \times_f X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{i}} &amp; {}^{\hat g}\nearrow
                    \\\
                    B
                    }
            %p
              commutes. To do so we notice that we obtain two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cones"} cones
              with tip
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %ul
              %li
                %p one is given by the morphisms
                %ol
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo →
                          %mi Z
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi f
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to Z \times_f X \to X
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi i
                          %mi B
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                          %mi Z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{i}{\to} B \stackrel{g}{\to} Z
                %p with universal morphism into the pullback being
                %ul
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo →
                          %mi Z
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi f
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to Z \times_f X
              %li
                %p the other by
                %ol
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi i
                          %mi B
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mover
                              %mi g
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mi Z
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi f
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{i}{\to} B \stackrel{\hat g}{\to} Z \times_f X \to X
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi i
                          %mi B
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                          %mi Z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{i}{\to} B \stackrel{g}{\to} Z
                    \.
                %p with universal morphism into the pullback being
                %ul
                  %li
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi i
                          %mi B
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mover
                              %mi g
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mi Z
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi f
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{i}{\to} B \stackrel{\hat g}{\to} Z \times_f X
                    \.
            %p
              The commutativity of the diagrams that we have established so far shows that the first and second morphisms here equal each other, respectively. By the fact that the universal morphism into a pullback diagram is
              %em unique
              this implies the required identity of morphisms.
            %p
              The other case is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
            %p
              %strong closure under (co-)products
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi s
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mi Proj
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{(A_s \overset{i_s}{\to} B_s) \in K Proj\}_{s \in S}
              be a set of elements of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mi Proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta[1]}
              are computed componentwise, their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              in this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
              is the universal morphism out of the coproduct of objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{s \in S}{\coprod} A_s
              induced via its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              by the set of morphisms
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_s
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi s
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi s
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi S
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi s
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} A_s
                    \\overset{(i_s)_{s\in S}}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} B_s
                    \\,.
            %p Now let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mrow
                                %mi s
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi S
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi s
                                  %msub
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi s
                                      %mo ∈
                                      %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mrow
                                %mi s
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi S
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} A_s &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(i_s)_{s\in S}}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in K}}
                    \\\
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} B_s
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    Y
                    }
            %p
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
              under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              of objects, hence by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the coproduct, this is equivalent to a set of commuting diagrams
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi A
                                  %mi s
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msubsup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo ∈
                                      %mi K
                                      %mi Proj
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi i
                                        %mi s
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msubsup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo ∈
                                      %mi K
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi f
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi B
                                  %mi s
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi Y
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    A_s &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i_s}}_{\mathllap{\in K Proj}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in K}}
                    \\\
                    B_s
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    Y
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\right\}_{s\in S}
                    \\,.
            %p
              By assumption, each of these has a lift
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell_s
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi A
                                  %mi s
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msubsup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo ∈
                                      %mi Proj
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi i
                                        %mi s
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi ℓ
                                      %mi s
                                %mo ↗
                              %mtd
                                %msubsup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo ∈
                                      %mi K
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi f
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi B
                                  %mi s
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi Y
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    A_s &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{i_s}}_{\mathllap{\in Proj}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;{}^{\ell_s}\nearrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in K}}
                    \\\
                    B_s
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    Y
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\right\}_{s\in S}
            %p
              is now itself a compatible
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the coproduct, this is equivalent to a lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\ell_s)_{s\in S}
              in the original square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mrow
                                %mi s
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi S
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi s
                                  %msub
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi s
                                      %mo ∈
                                      %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi ℓ
                                  %mi s
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi s
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi S
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi K
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mrow
                                %mi s
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi S
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} A_s &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(i_s)_{s\in S}}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;{}^{(\ell_s)_{s\in S}}\nearrow&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in K}}
                    \\\
                    \\underset{s \in S}{\sqcup} B_s
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This shows that the coproduct of the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_s
              has the left lifting property against all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in K
              and is hence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mi Proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K Proj
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              is about factoring morphisms into
              = succeed "-cofibrations" do
